{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261101T131902Z-266dd49f", "ts": "2026-11-01T13:21:03Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "feature/change-log-fragments-advisory", "build": "39144ab1f1d5"}, "body": {"base_commit": "9a2eb20e0faf65b5ceb08c03651ccb84300bcc50", "base_tree": "1bd002c3c53cdf6b194d903bbbb13583dfba776a", "head_tree": "d936cb4dd59bb90d27a7e325eb78569278cce76b", "head_commit": "13330f64afe5ef961b3b4c77f2f369031c4bd831", "dispatch_commit": "13330f64afe5ef961b3b4c77f2f369031c4bd831", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py", "plugin/lib/probe_families.py", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md", "tests/test_change_record_probes.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/changes/change-log-fragments-advisory.md", "plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py", "plugin/lib/probe_families.py", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md", "tests/test_change_record_probes.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/changes/change-log-fragments-advisory.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "Advisory tells repos that already carry merge=union that their merges conflict on the log", "recommendation": "The probe fires whether or not `.prawduct/change-log.md` already has `merge=union` (the remedy prawduct used to recommend, so many legacy repos have it), but trigger_summary says unconditionally that 'every branch edits the same file and merges conflict there'. For a union-attributed repo that sentence is false; the real cost there is the union harm (archived entries resurfacing). Either reword it so it holds in both states (for example, 'every branch edits the same file, which either conflicts at merge or needs the union line that can bring archived entries back'), or branch on `gitstate.git_merge_attribute` only for the text and keep the evidence tuple unchanged so the id stays stable. The fragment's consumer note makes the same claim.", "files": ["plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "The prerequisite edge to change-log-union-merge is pinned as a string, never as an ordering both probes produce", "recommendation": "The test asserts `prerequisite_of[0][0] == \"gitattributes:change-log-union-merge\"`. The edge fails soft, so a renamed feature or type would leave it inert with that test still green. Add one test that registers both probes (register_all) on a committed-log repo with no union line, checks that both types fire, and checks that the declared key equals the union advisory's `<feature>:<type>`. A briefing `_order_advisories` assertion would be better still. That pins the change fragment's 'ordered before change-log-union-merge' claim as behaviour.", "files": ["tests/test_change_record_probes.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "change_record_probes builds the same AdvisoryCandidate twice, varying only owner_action, and re-derives the release string change_migrate already formats", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The cause is a branch on the pin that was written as two full constructions instead of two owner_action strings. Choose owner_action inside the `if pinned` and construct the candidate once, so type, recommended_action, prerequisite_of, priority and the 'doctor check #22 is the one home' comment exist at one site, not one of them on just one branch. If that is done, `first = \"v\" + \".\".join(map(str, FRAGMENT_READERS_RELEASE))` (also at change_migrate.py:110) could be a single name exported by change_migrate. Optional: today the two branches agree and the tests pin both, so nobody acts wrongly on the current code.", "files": ["plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Doctor #22's new sentence says the advisory 'reports the same state', but the probe's trigger is narrower: a committed log only, and no answer when git cannot be asked", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Check #22 grades on '.prawduct/change-log.md exists', but the probe deliberately stays quiet on an untracked log. So 'the same state' is a little stronger than the code. Nothing reads this as a predicate, and doctor still grades on its own trigger, so no maintainer acts wrongly on it. If it is touched again, make it relational ('reports this state when the log is committed') rather than adding a sentence beside it. No edit is wanted for this landing.", "files": ["plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "The new probe's could-not-look path is silent, unlike every other probe that returns None", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. When `gitstate.git_path_is_tracked` returns None, `probe_change_log_fragments_available` returns None (could not look) and prints nothing. `advisory_store.run_probes` relies on the probe to report this: its comment says \"A probe that could not look prints its own NOTE naming what went unchecked\", and run_probes prints nothing for a plain None. All eight other `return None  # could not look` sites in plugin/lib/*_probes.py print a stderr NOTE first (adhoc_delegate, git_hygiene, evidence_size, gitattributes x3, retired_state, stranded_branch). Here a broken index or a missing git means a legacy repo is quietly never told about the migration, and nobody can see that the check did not run. The hook-surface learning applies: \"Pick each fallback's direction from the invariant it protects: an unknown bucket blocks, degraded advice names its consequence\". Fix: before `return None`, print a NOTE such as `NOTE: change-record probe skipped: git could not say whether .prawduct/change-log.md is committed \u2014 a repo still on the single-file log would go unadvised this session` to sys.stderr. In `test_could_not_look_outside_a_repo`, use capsys to assert that the NOTE appears.", "files": ["plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py", "tests/test_change_record_probes.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog reconciliation: no open item resolved; C-B3 doctor-area item #120 is adjacent to the new pin-first owner text", "recommendation": "Scope: none (mandated cross-check). `cache-query affecting` over the four subject files returns only #928 (host adapters), which this change does not touch. Searching the open set for change-log, fragment, migrate and doctor finds nothing this change resolves; #834 (derive the change-log entry at merge) stays open. C-B3: the change touches doctor, where #120 (\"doctor: detect a stale ref-pinned marketplace\") is open. The new advisory's pinned-case owner_action now tells a repo pinned below v3.7.2 to move its pin, which is one face of #120's stale-pin concern. Check whether #120 should mention this advisory. #563 (doctor checks record no fired event) was already dispositioned for doctor-area changes and is not raised again.", "files": ["plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md", "plugin/lib/change_record_probes.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings cross-check: rules read; one warned-against pattern, folded into the logging finding", "recommendation": "Scope: none (mandated cross-check). The read list from `learnings-files --for-diff` is core.md, authoring.md, hook-surface.md, release.md and tests.md. Only one rule is reintroduced as a pattern: hook-surface's \"Pick each fallback's direction ...\", which is already cited in the could-not-look finding and does not need a second finding. Three rules are followed. tests.md \"An advisory's printed recommendation ships to every consumer repo \u2014 test its EFFECT\": `test_following_the_advice_resolves_it` runs the migration and checks that the probe goes quiet. authoring.md \"Never write a present-tense state claim\": the fragment's 28/2 sibling-repo count is dated 2026-11-01. core.md \"A channel that is produced and never consumed is a DEFECT\": the advisory is consumed by the briefing, and doctor's routing table names it. This change adds or edits no learnings rules.", "fid": "R-7"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 6}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `feature/change-log-fragments-advisory`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "9a2eb20e0faf65b5ceb08c03651ccb84300bcc50", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/changes/change-log-fragments-advisory.md", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-01T13:19:03Z"}}

